              "AcceptedStatsName": "Name n Slope Intercept SEslope SEintercept R2 RMSE NSE ME MAE RSR",
              "POName": "PredictedObserved",
              "Name": "Tests",
              "ResourceName": null,
              "Children": [
                {
                  "$type": "Models.Memo, Models",
                  "Text": "<br>\r\n__Where:__\n\r\n - n: The number of PO (predicted-observed) pairs for the given variable;  \r\n - Slope: The slope of the straight line linear regression. A perfect fit would have a value of 1;  \r\n - Intercept: The intercept of the straight line linear regression. A perfect fit would have a value of 0;  \r\n - SEslope: Standard error in the slope;  \r\n - SEintercept: Standard error in the intercept.;  \r\n - R2: The value for the coefficient of determination. It varies between 0 and 1, where 1 is a perfect fit;  \r\n - RMSE: Root Mean Squared Error. 0 is a perfect fit. Values less than half the standard deviation of the observed data are acceptable;  \r\n - NSE: Nash-Sutcliffe Efficiency. Indicates how well the PO data fits the 1:1 line. Ranges from -âˆž to 1 with 1 being the optimal value while values  between 0 and 1 are generally viewed as acceptable. Values < 0 indicate unacceptable model performance;  \r\n - ME: Mean Error between predicted and observed values. 0 is a perfect fit;  \r\n - MAE: Mean Absolute Error. 0 is a perfect fit. Values less than half the standard deviation of the observed data are acceptable;  \r\n - RSR: Ratio between the RMSE and the standard deviation of observations. 0 is a perfect fit;  \r\n\r\n",
                  "Name": "Note",
                  "ResourceName": null,
                  "Children": [],
                  "Enabled": true,
                  "ReadOnly": false
                }
              ],
              "Enabled": true,
              "ReadOnly": false
