              "Children": [
                {
                  "$type": "Models.Factorial.Experiment, Models",
                  "DisabledSimNames": null,
                  "Name": "FRNLRuakura",
                  "ResourceName": null,
                  "Children": [
                    {
                      "$type": "Models.Memo, Models",
                      "Text": "This simulation setup was based on field trials performed at DairyNZ's Scott Farm, in Ruakura, New Zealand, between 2014 and 2016.  The experiment was part of the FRNL (Forages for Reduced Nitrogen Leaching) program and the data is basically unpublished (references will be added when they become available).  \r\nThe experiment consisted of six fertiliser treatments (N rates of 0, 50, 100, 200, 350 and 500 kg/ha/yr) in three replicates, and measurements comprised yield and quality indicators (here N content is used).  \r\nObserved data supplied by Grant Edwards, Lincoln University.\r\n\r\nThe soil at the experimental site was a Horotiu silt loam (an Orthic Allophanic soil; USDA: Typic Udivitrand), the parameters required were inferred using data from the New Zealand National Soils Database (Landcare Research).  \r\nWeather data was obtained from nearby Ruakura weather station (NIWA).\r\n",
                      "Name": "Memo",
                      "ResourceName": null,
                      "Children": [],
                      "Enabled": true,
                      "ReadOnly": false
